Well, after having lost a good character to YASD (yet another stupid death),
   I've had a few musings and a few questions.  I guess that there are some
   implicit spoilers, too, so...


If you read a cursed scroll of enchant weapon while confused, perhaps it ought
   to polymorph the weapon you're wielding.  However, this removes the only
   way to un-rustproof a weapon.

Ditto with cursed scrolls of enchant armor when confused - maybe they should
   polymorph a random piece of armor.

Is there anything that would keep me from getting an artifact?  I was running
   a Valkyrie (chaotic) and I expended a wand of create monster and a spellbook
   of the same next to an altar, trying to get an artifact, and while I got a
   goodly number of "You see a 4-leaf clover at your feet"'s, I got nada in
   the way of "stuff".  I'm pretty sure that I was stridently alighned - I
   hadn't killed any peaceful monsters (or are chaotic players _supposed_ to
   do that?).  Does it matter if a pet kills a peaceful monster?  What if one
   peaceful monster kills another due to a ring of conflict?

I'm administering the game on a UNIX box and every now and then I get a lot 
   of "alock.*" files left in the directory.  I know what these files _are_,
   but I'm wondering if there's a way of finding out who they belonged to -
   so I could email and ask if they're actually playing the game or if the
   files are dead and should be trashed.  I've tried "od -s" on the file, but
   I can't find any definitive way of determining whse "*lock.*" files are 
   whose other than remembering what certain people tend to call their pets.

Thanks.

